| Data Store | [Configuration row](resources/datastore_row.md) | [Tables](data-sources/datastore_tables.md), [table schema](data-sources/datastore_table.md) |
| API Gateway | [Gateway](resources/api_gateway.md), [complete ruleset](resources/api_gateway_ruleset.md) | None |
| Job Scheduling | [Webhook](resources/webhook_cron.md), [Job Function](resources/function_cron.md), [AppSail](resources/appsail_cron.md) | [Job pools](data-sources/job_pools.md) |
| Projects | [Project (experimental)](resources/project.md) | [Project](data-sources/project.md), [projects](data-sources/projects.md) |
| Authentication | [User role assignment (experimental)](resources/auth_user_role.md) | [User access metadata](data-sources/auth_user.md) |
| Cache | None | [Segments](data-sources/cache_segments.md) |
| File Store | [File (deprecated)](resources/filestore_file.md) | [Folders (deprecated)](data-sources/filestore_folders.md) |

Tables, columns, indexes, buckets, job pools, roles and permissions must already
exist. AppSail containers, explicit scaling controls, custom domains, Production
promotion, Authentication setup and Connections provisioning are not implemented.
The [service expansion guide](guides/service_expansion.md),
[Authentication and Connections guide](guides/authentication_connections.md) and
[Project ownership and recovery guide](guides/project_management.md)
explain the supported subsets and verification limits.

## Lifecycle and State

Use exact string IDs, matching data center/environment settings and exclusive
ownership of each resource across Terraform states and other deployment tools.
For Functions and AppSail, import an existing deployment instead of adopting it
by name. Gateway rulesets own all custom rules; omitted rules are removed.

~> **Note:** Values marked sensitive are hidden in normal output but still
remain in Terraform state. This includes environment variables, configuration
rows/items and scheduling request values. Use protected state storage. Keep
customer transactions and changing application records outside Terraform.

Terraform deploys prebuilt archives; it does not build dependencies or normally
invoke your application. Successful deployment readback verifies persistence,
not application health, end-user authentication setup or Production readiness.
Schedules default to disabled.

Read requests retry temporary failures with bounded backoff and `Retry-After`
handling. Ambiguous writes are not automatically replayed. If a create succeeds
remotely but its response is lost, inspect the service and import it before
retrying. Import identities and replacement behavior are documented per resource.

## Troubleshooting

| Symptom | Check |
| --- | --- |
| Provider cannot be installed | Use the local development override; a public Registry release is not available yet. |
| Missing or mixed credentials | Select exactly one authentication mode and review inherited `CATALYST_` variables. |
| Unauthorized or forbidden API call | Check token expiry, required scopes, account data center, organization and project access. |
| Missing table, bucket, role or job pool | Provision the documented prerequisite in the selected project/environment. Discovery does not create it. |
| Existing deployment name | Import the existing object; do not create a second Terraform owner. |
| App URL exists but requests fail | Check the application's entry point, built dependencies, listening address/port and application permissions. |
| Missing organization or routing mismatch | Supply the original explicit organization, data center and environment. Changing routing does not migrate an object; see [environment isolation](guides/environments.md). |
| Legacy state has no routing binding | Review and apply a refresh-only plan under the original routing before mutation; see [state migration](guides/environments.md#upgrade-existing-state). |
| Project creation rejected | The tested OAuth context rejected direct creation with a CLI-version message; the inspected CLI uses console-assisted creation. Use a console-created project through a data source or deliberate import; see [project creation limits](guides/project_management.md#unblock-live-project-creation). |

